.venv/
uv.lock

# The reference recordings stay out. `bake-lines` does not need them, only
# re-cloning does, and re-cloning is non-deterministic anyway: it produces a
# different voice rather than the same one, so shipping them buys no
# reproducibility. `samples/*.wav` alone missed `samples/clean/`.
samples/**
!samples/README.md

# Piper stand-in models. Large, and downloaded by the tool on demand.
voices/

# Generated audio. Every one of these is reproducible from a command.
out/

# The cloned voice states. `out/` alone did not cover `out-real/`, which is the
# directory the README actually tells you to use, so four safetensors files
# reached a public repository in f243da9 and are still in its history. A cloned
# voice is a portable model of a real person: anyone holding one can make that
# person say anything, and the people recorded agreed to voice a game, which is
# not the same thing. This rule stops the next one; it does not untrack the four
# already committed, because .gitignore never has.
out-real/
preview*/
audition*/
shift/
clone-slots/
listen/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
